nter this stronghold, although it is a favourite place with you. Herein dwell many forest-rangers, wifeless and having wives. And we are really afraid of them, avaricious, and formerly deprived of their wealth by us.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-19-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4019015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"54465b92e37de3ba9134ab7b232963aa80f54adfcd56b505fb7694c980156970","compact":"01f184d596d2ede2fc92a42f057052fb3ab886dfbe9ffd10ff6ba82537916d81","nasal":"d771c75c6d572b9ef1d751827d63f495085497a509bfbec3c78eb702456f53cc"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-19-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":19,"verse":16,"english":"O you having a fine countenance, the monkeys shall enter this stronghold, although it is a favourite place with you. Herein dwell many forest-rangers, wifeless and having wives. And we are really afraid of them, avaricious, and formerly deprived of their wealth by us.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.587,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-19-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4019016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"64b100754a45d9944b34aaf66228431b49dea26e4c30fd916b11400858f15543","compact":"467a2b7df3ddc63a30b1824f0245fc61aa8ac9f60ffcbee48594a822781f6e9b","nasal":"3570cc6029b01378e12f306ad0114d7c55a78eb6af7cf53f954bc0e1938b3e28"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-19-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":19,"verse":17,"english":"Hearing those words of the monkeys, lying at a little distance, that lady, smiling sweet, spoke to them, words worthy of herself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-19-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4019017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891